  "id": "COMPOUND:34580 - PROTEIN:1146",
  "verbalization": "Isoswinholide B appears to have multiple targets that ultimately lead to the Dr hemagglutinin structural subunit, suggesting a complex network of interactions. The evidence indicates that Isoswinholide B acts on U-87 MG cells, which are targeted by both Isoswinholide B and Nomilin, and that Nomilin in turn targets Dr hemagglutinin. Additionally, Isoswinholide B is also linked to another target, (2S)-3',4'-Dihydroxy-6,7-Dimethoxyflavan, which also targets Dr hemagglutinin. This suggests that Isoswinholide B may exert its effects through a series of intermediate pathways, potentially involving mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 13, which is targeted by Isoswinholide B and in turn targets Dr hemagglutinin. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Isoswinholide B influences cellular processes that ultimately modulate the structure and function of Dr hemagglutinin. The evidence supports a role for Isoswinholide B in the regulation of Dr hemagglutinin, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
